  "considered": [
    "The previous set: a child's crayon flowers and sun shared on Pixabay by Efraimstochter (Pixabay Content License). Retired because it made the product read as a children's app.",
    "Pixabay, jinjinjinjin, \"Hand Painted, Watercolor, Flower\" series (https://pixabay.com/illustrations/hand-painted-watercolor-flower-2540639/ and siblings 2540635 to 2540641), Pixabay Content License. Real hand-painted wildflowers, but bold greeting-card gouache and wreath layouts, louder than the interface.",
    "Pixabay poppy and meadow watercolors from 2022 onward (for example 7509834, 7543125, 7746724). Rejected: Pixabay marks several as AI generated, and the rest could not be told apart with confidence.",
    "Mary Vaux Walcott, Group of Flowers (SAAM 1970.355.12) and California Poppy (1970.355.303). Lovely, but the bouquet is painted to the edges and the poppies are too saturated for a calm strip.",
    "Mary Vaux Walcott, Sun Dial Lupine (SAAM 1970.355.345). Painted to the edges of the sheet, so its leaves end in straight cuts; left out of the strips.",
    "Mary Vaux Walcott, Perennial Gaillardia (SAAM 1970.355.691). A beautiful painting, but its saturated yellow pulled the eye out of the strip.",
    "Mary Vaux Walcott, Golden Fleabane (SAAM 1970.355.133). Tried as the approval flower; at 40 pixels its gray leaves turned to a smudge, so a single wind poppy took its place."
  ],
